{"name":"Orestes","hex":"#9e9b85","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Orestes","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Heteropterygidae – several stick insects."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The son of Agamemnon and Clytemnestra, who killed his mother, avenging his father's death, and was then pursued by the Furies.","A region of Macedonia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Orestes"}],"entries":[{"title":"Orestes","blocks":[{"text":"In Greek mythology, Orestes or Orestis was the son of Agamemnon and Clytemnestra, and the brother of Electra and Iphigenia. He was also known by the patronymic Agamemnonides (Ἀγαμεμνονίδης), meaning \"son of Agamemnon.\" He is the subject of multiple Ancient Greek plays, which depict his revenge, madness, and ritual purification."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Orestes_Apollo_Louvre_Cp710.jpg/330px-Orestes_Apollo_Louvre_Cp710.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orestes","wikidata":"Q192407"},{"title":"Orestes (play)","blocks":[{"text":"Orestes (408 BCE) is an Ancient Greek play by Euripides that follows the events of Orestes after he had murdered his mother."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Euripides%2C_Orestes%2C_Oxford%2C_MS._Barocci_120.jpg/330px-Euripides%2C_Orestes%2C_Oxford%2C_MS._Barocci_120.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orestes_(play)","wikidata":"Q663886"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Orestes_Delphi_BM_GR1917.12-10.1.jpg/500px-Orestes_Delphi_BM_GR1917.12-10.1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Orestes_Delphi_BM_GR1917.12-10.1.jpg/1280px-Orestes_Delphi_BM_GR1917.12